# ==============================================================================
# sdl3-native-tools/.gitignore
# ==============================================================================
#
# LINE 1 IS LOAD-BEARING - DO NOT DELETE IT.
#
# The repository-root .gitignore is the standard Visual Studio / .NET one. It
# ignores names that also occur inside the vendored SDL source tree, for example:
#
#     [Xx]64/            -> SDL/VisualC/... project output folder names
#     [Aa][Rr][Mm]64/    -> any arm64 folder in the SDL tree
#     [Dd]ebug/  [Rr]elease/  [Oo]ut/  [Ll]og/  bld/  [Oo]bj/ ...
#     *.env              -> linux/pins.env
#
# Without the "!*" below, such files would be silently left out of every
# commit, and the vendored snapshot (or the build pins) would not be there for
# the next person who cloned this repository. A nested .gitignore takes
# precedence over the ones above it, so re-including everything here and then
# re-ignoring only what this folder genuinely produces is the correct fix - and
# it keeps the root .gitignore untouched.
#
# SDL/.gitignore is UPSTREAM's own file and is part of the unmodified snapshot.
# It is deeper than this one, so it still applies inside SDL/ - that is correct,
# because it only names build products that are not part of upstream's tree.
#
# Verify at any time with:
#     git check-ignore -v sdl3-native-tools/linux/pins.env
#     git check-ignore -v sdl3-native-tools/SDL/src/video/x11/SDL_x11video.c
#         -> should print nothing (i.e. the file is NOT ignored)
# ==============================================================================

# Re-include everything under this folder, overriding the root .gitignore.
!*
!*/

# --- what this folder really does produce, and must not commit ---------------

# Built native libraries, unstripped copies, smoke-test binaries, SHA256SUMS.
# ONE tree, shared by every platform build, so all RIDs land side by side.
#
# THE LEADING SLASH MATTERS: without it the pattern would match ANY directory
# named "output" at any depth, including inside the vendored SDL tree.
# NOTE THE TRAILING /* RATHER THAN A BARE /output/. A directory that is itself
# excluded is never descended into, so a later "!" rule could never re-include
# the README inside it. Excluding the CONTENTS leaves the directory visible,
# and the negation below then works.
/output/*

# ...except the placeholder README that explains what goes there.
!/output/README.txt

# Local scratch that the scripts may leave behind.
*.tmp
*.log
build-scratch/

# Finder droppings. Needed explicitly: the "!*" above re-includes everything
# under this folder and so overrides any .DS_Store rule inherited from the root
# or from a user's global gitignore.
.DS_Store
